---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { PAYHIP_AFFILIATE_URL } from '../data/site';
import { routes } from '../i18n/ui';
---

<PageLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Affiliate links"
  description="Why some links on lord.crofte.fr are affiliate links, how they are signalled, which programmes I take part in, and what it changes for you."
  alternates={routes.affiliate}
  updated={new Date('2026-10-29')}
>
  <p>
    Some links on this website are affiliate links. If you buy something after following one of them, the seller pays me
    a small commission. It costs you nothing extra, and it helps keep the guides free.
  </p>

  <h2>How to recognise them</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every page containing at least one affiliate link says so in a notice at the top of the page.</li>
    <li>In the code, these links carry <code>rel="sponsored"</code>, as search engines ask.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Programmes I take part in</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Payhip</strong>, the platform behind my shop. If you want to sell your own patterns, my
      <a href={PAYHIP_AFFILIATE_URL} rel="sponsored noopener">Payhip referral link</a>
      is the one to use.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Amazon</strong>. As an Amazon Associate, I earn from qualifying purchases.</li>
    <li><strong>AliExpress</strong>, for some tools and hardware.</li>
    <li>Some <strong>partner shops</strong> also give discount codes to my readers. A code may earn me a commission too.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>My commitment</h2>
  <p>
    I only recommend tools and materials I use or would use myself. An affiliate programme never decides what I
    recommend, and I also link to products that earn me nothing.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
